hexagon: skip the zero terms of the forward substitution of version 2

The cost

Version 2 of the chunked gated delta net kernel sends each chunk with a zero coefficient in the forward
substitution to a second solve with the arithmetic of version 1. That solve converts each product and
each sum to IEEE f32 at once and does one row at a time. A strong decay flushes the coefficients far from
the diagonal to zero, and a small key product times a moderate decay also flushes to zero. Thus the 4B
shape with gates from -0.5 also sends chunks to that solve, and the kernel has two solves with different
rounding.

The change

- gdn_c2_solve does not run a term with a zero coefficient. The probe of stage gdnk3 (2026-09-25, the
  v79 NPU of the phone) shows the cause of the values near 2^105 that the qfloat solve gave for such
  chunks:
    - A qfloat product with a zero operand gives the qf32 bits 0x00000080 (+2^-22) or 0xffffff80
      (-2^-22), for each other operand, zero included.
    - A sum of 16 such products with mixed signs (the form of the solve with zero coefficients) gives
      0x400000e9, which is about 2^106 in f32. The float64 value is 0.
    - The same sums with coefficients of 0 or 0.5, and with 2^-60 in place of 0, agree with a float64
      reference to 1 or 2 ulp.
    - The products of normal operands are correct down to 2^-149. 2^-80 * 2^-80 gives a wrapped qf32
      value, thus the multiply operands keep the flush below 2^-50 (gdn_c2_ftz).
- The zeros of a row usually come first, because the decay decreases with the distance from the
  diagonal. For each pair of rows, a vector max finds the last zero coefficient. The terms up to it go one
  at a time with a test of each coefficient. The terms after it go in pairs with no test, as before.
- Each chunk takes gdn_c2_solve. gdn_c2_solve_f32, the zero mask of phase solve and the macro
  GDN_C2_SOLVE_F32_ALWAYS go.
- The state goes through gdn_c2_ftz one time, in phase begin. gdn_c2_state_row flushed it at each update
  when it read it, and it still flushes each state that it stores.

The results

The kernel lab (tools/htp-lab, target gdnk, the v79 timing model, 12 heads of 128, 512 tokens, 6 threads,
--hmx 0), the cycles of the kernel functions on the threads, HEAD fa1530b against this patch:
                        HEAD      this patch
    gates from -0.5     4.94 M    4.73 M (-4.2 %)
    gates from -20      5.76 M    5.71 M (-1.0 %)
With gates from -0.5 the solve phase goes from 1.62 M to 1.52 M cycles, and the state update goes from
0.91 M to 0.72 M. The simulator gives exact zeros for the qfloat products with a zero operand, thus the
lab cannot show the defect of the phone. The functional runs of the patch before give the same NMSE with
this patch (9 runs of 70 to 512 tokens, gates from -0.5 to -8, 1 to 5 snapshot slots, with and without
the norm). A run with gates from -20 (165 tokens, 5 slots, the norm) gives 3.1e-07 for the output. The
target gdnsolve (gates from -0.5, -8 and -20) gives a worst error of 3.8e-09 or less.

On the phone (HTP0, Qwen3.5-4B Q8_0, stages gdnk3 and gdnk3p of 2026-09-25) A is HEAD fa1530b and B is
this patch, with the same libraries apart from the Hexagon backend:
- test-backend-ops passes the 82 cases of the gated delta net ops with the q/k norm inside and without it.
- The KL divergence of the prefill path against the naive x86 base (4 chunks of 512) is 0.000617 +-
  0.000045 for B and 0.000602 +- 0.000042 for A. The decode path gives 0.000534 +- 0.000077 for B.
- The probe log of each phase (gates from -20, one and four chunks) has no value that is not finite. 1927
  to 1945 of the 2016 coefficients of a chunk are zero.
- test-backend-ops perf, the median of 2 rounds:
      case                                    A          B
      16 k heads, 32 v heads, 1024 tokens     3092 us    3083 us
      32 heads, 1024 tokens, gates from -20   4116 us    4044 us
- llama-bench, 5 rounds with A and B in turn, the rounds that the runner did not mark for a change of
  the CPU caps (A 3, B 4): pp512 1159.5 t/s for A and 1164.4 t/s for B, pp1024 1111.5 t/s for A and
  1123.9 t/s for B. The paired difference is -0.1 % for pp512 and +0.9 % for pp1024.
Thus the speed does not change on the phone. The solve of version 1 was not the cause of the difference
between the 2762 us of version 2 before the flushes (stage gdnk of 2026-09-24) and its time with them.

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 with the patches of patches/series above this one.

